# VOID Welkin: English names and tooltips (generated by tools/options.py)

profile.LOW=Low
profile.MEDIUM=Medium
profile.HIGH=High
profile.comment=Quick settings that set the options costing the most. Low: for older or laptop graphics: no shadows, one cloud layer, simpler haze, mist and cave fog, no distant rain (about 2 ms at 1080p). Medium: the intended look: shadows, two cloud layers, puddles, distant rain and far mist (about 4 ms). High: sharper, longer, softer-edged shadows, all cloud layers to 64 km, near reflections in water (about 5.5 ms).

screen.LIGHT=Light and shadows
screen.LIGHT.comment=Sunlight, shadows, torch light and glowing blocks.
screen.SKY=Sky
screen.SKY.comment=The sky's pixel grid, the sun, the moon and the stars.
screen.AIR=Haze and mist
screen.AIR.comment=The air over the land: distance haze coloured by the country you are in, and valley mist.
screen.CLOUDS=Clouds
screen.CLOUDS.comment=Block clouds shaped by the weather.
screen.WATER=Water
screen.WATER.comment=The water's surface, its texture and reflections.
screen.WEATHER=Weather and seasons
screen.WEATHER.comment=Wet ground, distant rain, frost and the light of each season.
screen.PLANTS=Plants and wind
screen.PLANTS.comment=How leaves, grass and water plants move in the wind.
screen.UNDERGROUND=Underground
screen.UNDERGROUND.comment=Cave fog, cave water, glowworm caves and damp walls.
screen.FAR=Far land
screen.FAR.comment=How the far land drawn by VOID LOD looks.
screen.LOOK=Colour and finish
screen.LOOK.comment=How gently light and the sky gather into soft bands.
screen.DEBUG=Debug
screen.DEBUG.comment=Views and switches for testing the shader. Leave these alone for normal play.

option.SHADOWS=Sun and moon shadows
option.SHADOWS.comment=Blocks and creatures near you cast shadows from the sun and the moon, and leaves and grass sway in them. Turning this off saves more time than any other option.

option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow detail
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=How finely shadows are drawn. Higher gives cleaner shadow edges on small things like fences and leaves, and costs more.
value.shadowMapResolution.1024=Low
value.shadowMapResolution.1536=Medium
value.shadowMapResolution.2048=High
value.shadowMapResolution.3072=Very high
value.shadowMapResolution.4096=Ultra

option.shadowDistance=Shadow distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far away blocks cast shadows from the shadow map. Past this, Far shadows take over from what is on screen, and the change is a smooth fade.
suffix.shadowDistance= blocks

option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow edges
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=How a shadow's edge softens. Natural is crisp at the foot of what casts it and widens with the distance from it, as real shadows do; Soft widens it more; Crisp keeps every edge sharp. Always smooth, with no grain.
value.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.0=Crisp
value.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.1=Natural
value.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.2=Soft

option.FAR_SHADOWS=Far shadows
option.FAR_SHADOWS.comment=Beyond the shadow distance, houses, trees, hills and the far land still cast long shadows, worked out from what is on screen. Something off the screen casts none there.

option.AMBIENT_OCCLUSION=Ambient occlusion
option.AMBIENT_OCCLUSION.comment=Corners, the feet of walls, eaves, the inside of tree crowns and the roots of grass sink into a soft, graded shade, worked out from the shapes around them, so open shade stays bright and sky-blue while every form reads. Smooth, with no grain.

option.sunPathRotation=Sun path tilt
option.sunPathRotation.comment=How far the path of the sun and moon leans south, so south-facing walls get the sun as they would in the north of the Earth. Vanilla is 0.
suffix.sunPathRotation= degrees

option.LIGHT_BANDS=Light bands
option.LIGHT_BANDS.comment=How many soft bands sky light and torch light fade through. The light stays a smooth gradient; Soft bands sets how much it gathers at each band.

option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH=Torch light strength
option.BLOCKLIGHT_STRENGTH.comment=How bright the light from torches, lanterns and other glowing blocks looks. The game's light levels do not change.

option.HANDHELD_LIGHT=Light from held items
option.HANDHELD_LIGHT.comment=A torch or other glowing item in your hand lights the area around you. This is only a look: mobs still see the real light level.

option.EMISSIVE_BLOCKS=Glowing pixels
option.EMISSIVE_BLOCKS.comment=The bright pixels of torches, lanterns, lava, glowing ores and cave growths glow in their own colour, even in the dark.

option.SKY_PIXEL_SUN=Pixel sun and moon
option.SKY_PIXEL_SUN.comment=Draws the sun and the moon, with all eight moon phases, as crisp pixel art in the sky instead of the vanilla pictures.

option.SUN_SIZE=Sun size
option.SUN_SIZE.comment=How large the sun is, in art pixels across its radius.

option.MOON_SIZE=Moon size
option.MOON_SIZE.comment=How large the moon is, in art pixels across its radius.

option.SKY_ART_PIXEL=Sun and moon pixel size
option.SKY_ART_PIXEL.comment=How big one pixel of the sun and moon art is. 94 matches one pixel of the vanilla sun.

option.SKY_TEXELS=Sky pixel grid
option.SKY_TEXELS.comment=How fine the grid the stars sit on is. Lower gives fewer, chunkier star pixels. The sky's colours are smooth whatever this is.

option.STAR_DENSITY=Number of stars
option.STAR_DENSITY.comment=How many stars fill a clear, moonless night.

option.STAR_TWINKLE=Twinkling stars
option.STAR_TWINKLE.comment=Now and then a star dims for a moment.

option.SUN_HALO=Sun ring
option.SUN_HALO.comment=A thin ring of pale light around the sun, one art pixel wide. There is no glow or bloom.

option.NIGHT_SKYLIGHT=Night sky light
option.NIGHT_SKYLIGHT.comment=How much light the night sky gives, as a share of the day's. VOID Gloam's dark nights then darken it further, as in the game.

option.HAZE_ENABLED=Distance haze
option.HAZE_ENABLED.comment=Faraway land fades into air coloured by the country you are in: blue-grey over wet lowlands, warm over dry ones, thin and blue in the mountains.

option.HAZE_STRENGTH=Haze strength
option.HAZE_STRENGTH.comment=How thick the haze is over hazy lands.
option.HAZE_NEAR_CLEAR=Clear near air
option.HAZE_NEAR_CLEAR.comment=Over how many blocks the land's haze sets in, so the near and middle land keep their full light and shade and only the distance takes the air's colour. 0 hazes the near land as much as the far.
value.HAZE_NEAR_CLEAR.0=Off
suffix.HAZE_NEAR_CLEAR= blocks

option.HAZE_SAMPLES=Haze detail
option.HAZE_SAMPLES.comment=How many points along each view the haze looks at to pick a country's colour. More blends borders between lands more smoothly.
value.HAZE_SAMPLES.2=Low
value.HAZE_SAMPLES.3=Medium
value.HAZE_SAMPLES.4=High

option.HAZE_RAIN=Haze in rain
option.HAZE_RAIN.comment=How much a downpour closes the distance in.

option.HAZE_ON_SKY=Haze on the sky
option.HAZE_ON_SKY.comment=The haze also tints the sky near the horizon, in the same colours as the land.

option.HAZE_SEA_LEVEL=Haze base height
option.HAZE_SEA_LEVEL.comment=The height the clear-air haze starts from. Leave at 63 unless the world's sea level is different.

option.VALLEY_MIST=Valley mist
option.VALLEY_MIST.comment=Mist gathers in valleys, hollows and along water at dawn and thins away by midday. Needs VOID Gloam.

option.MIST_THICKNESS=Mist thickness
option.MIST_THICKNESS.comment=How thick valley mist is.

option.MIST_SAMPLES=Mist detail
option.MIST_SAMPLES.comment=How many points across the land the mist looks at to find the hollows it fills. More gives the mist a truer shape.
value.MIST_SAMPLES.2=Low
value.MIST_SAMPLES.3=Medium
value.MIST_SAMPLES.4=High

option.CLOUDS=Block clouds
option.CLOUDS.comment=Solid clouds made of blocks, drawn by the shader and shaped by the weather. Off brings back the normal Minecraft clouds.

option.CLOUD_QUALITY=Cloud quality
option.CLOUD_QUALITY.comment=How far the finest cloud blocks reach and how far clouds are drawn before they turn into flat sheets.
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.1=Low
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.2=Medium
value.CLOUD_QUALITY.3=High

option.CLOUD_SHADOWS=Cloud shadows
option.CLOUD_SHADOWS.comment=Clouds cast large, slow-moving shadows on the land. Off, or shadows from the main layer, the main and low layers, or all three.
value.CLOUD_SHADOWS.0=Off
value.CLOUD_SHADOWS.1=Main layer
value.CLOUD_SHADOWS.2=Main and low
value.CLOUD_SHADOWS.3=All layers

option.CLOUD_FAIR=Fair-weather cloud
option.CLOUD_FAIR.comment=How much of a fair sky still has cloud. 34 gives about as many scattered clouds as vanilla.
suffix.CLOUD_FAIR=%

option.WS_RIPPLES=Water surface
option.WS_RIPPLES.comment=Flat water, smooth ripples that move with the wind, or ripples plus rings where rain falls.
value.WS_RIPPLES.0=Flat
value.WS_RIPPLES.1=Wind ripples
value.WS_RIPPLES.2=Ripples and rain

option.WS_WATER_TEXTURE=Vanilla water texture
option.WS_WATER_TEXTURE.comment=How much of Minecraft's own water texture shows through the shader's water.
suffix.WS_WATER_TEXTURE=%

option.WS_CAUSTICS=Light under water
option.WS_CAUSTICS.comment=Rippling lines of sunlight on the ground under water, moving with the waves. Needs sun and moon shadows.

option.WS_WATER_SSR=Near reflections
option.WS_WATER_SSR.comment=Water close to you also reflects nearby land and trees, not just the sky. Costs about 0.3 ms.

option.WET_ENABLED=Wet ground
option.WET_ENABLED.comment=Rain darkens the ground and it dries out slowly afterwards. Sand and soil soak up more than stone.

option.WET_PUDDLES=Puddles
option.WET_PUDDLES.comment=Pixel puddles shine on open flat ground while it is wet.

option.WET_PUDDLE_REACH=Puddle distance
option.WET_PUDDLE_REACH.comment=How far away puddles are still drawn.
suffix.WET_PUDDLE_REACH= blocks

option.WF_CURTAINS=Distant rain
option.WF_CURTAINS.comment=Grey curtains of rain hang under faraway rain clouds and travel with the weather.

option.WF_CURTAIN_STEPS=Distant rain detail
option.WF_CURTAIN_STEPS.comment=How many weather cells each view checks for rain. More finds thin, faraway showers too.

option.WF_CURTAIN_REACH=Distant rain reach
option.WF_CURTAIN_REACH.comment=How far away rain curtains are still drawn, in blocks.
value.WF_CURTAIN_REACH.16384.0=16 km
value.WF_CURTAIN_REACH.32768.0=32 km
value.WF_CURTAIN_REACH.65536.0=64 km
option.WS_SHORE_WET=Wet shores
option.WS_SHORE_WET.comment=A darker wet band on the land along the water's edge. Needs VOID Gloam.

option.WS_FROST=Frost
option.WS_FROST.comment=Frost on the blocks' pixels on cold mornings, melting by mid-morning, and a few glints on frost and snow in the sun.

option.WS_SEASON_LIGHT=Seasonal light
option.WS_SEASON_LIGHT.comment=A low winter sun with cooler shade, and warmer light in autumn. Needs VOID Gloam.

option.WAVING_LEAVES=Moving leaves
option.WAVING_LEAVES.comment=Leaves move with the wind. With VOID Gloam the wind changes with the weather.

option.WAVING_PLANTS=Moving plants
option.WAVING_PLANTS.comment=Grass, flowers, crops, hanging vines and moss move with the wind.

option.WAVING_WATER_PLANTS=Moving water plants
option.WAVING_WATER_PLANTS.comment=Seagrass and kelp sway in the water, and lily pads bob.

option.WAVE_STRENGTH=Wind strength
option.WAVE_STRENGTH.comment=How far leaves and plants move. They never move more than two texture pixels.

option.UG_FOG=Cave fog
option.UG_FOG.comment=Caves fill with a smooth fog that closes in tight passages and reaches far in great caverns and over buried seas. Needs VOID Gloam for all but a plain cave fog.

option.UG_FOG_SAMPLES=Cave fog detail
option.UG_FOG_SAMPLES.comment=How many points along each view the cave fog looks at to tell passages from caverns. More follows the shape of the cave more closely.
value.UG_FOG_SAMPLES.2=Low
value.UG_FOG_SAMPLES.3=Medium
value.UG_FOG_SAMPLES.4=High

option.UG_FOG_DENSITY=Cave fog strength
option.UG_FOG_DENSITY.comment=How thick cave fog is.

option.UG_FOG_BRIGHTNESS=Cave fog brightness
option.UG_FOG_BRIGHTNESS.comment=How bright cave fog and mist are drawn. How dark caves are for play does not change.

option.UG_WATER_KINDS=Cave water colours
option.UG_WATER_KINDS.comment=Underground water takes the colour of its kind: river, buried sea or a realm's lake.

option.UG_WATER_MIST=Mist over cave water
option.UG_WATER_MIST.comment=Mist rises over great underground rivers, low fog lies on buried seas, and a haze hangs over lava.

option.UG_GLOWWORMS=Glowworm caves
option.UG_GLOWWORMS.comment=Caves hung with glowworm silk glow a soft blue-green under the roof, with tiny specks of light on the roof itself.

option.UG_DAMP=Damp walls
option.UG_DAMP.comment=Darker, damp walls with drip streaks where water drips from the roof.

option.UG_AMBIENT=Cave air light
option.UG_AMBIENT.comment=A faint light in each underground realm's own colour, a little brighter in great caverns than in passages. How dark caves are for play does not change.

option.FAR_TEXTURE=Far land texture
option.FAR_TEXTURE.comment=Gives the far land drawn by VOID LOD a faint pixel texture on the world's grid, getting coarser with distance and fading out into the haze.

option.FAR_TEXTURE_PIXELS=Far texture size
option.FAR_TEXTURE_PIXELS.comment=How many screen pixels one far texture pixel covers before it doubles in size. Smaller is finer.
suffix.FAR_TEXTURE_PIXELS= px

option.FAR_FADE=Far fade
option.FAR_FADE.comment=The far land fades smoothly into the horizon towards the edge of what is drawn.

option.WF_FAR_MIST=Far valley mist
option.WF_FAR_MIST.comment=Valley mist carries on into the hollows of the faraway land, past the near mist.

option.WF_FAR_HAZE=Far haze
option.WF_FAR_HAZE.comment=The haze carries on over the far land drawn by VOID LOD, thicker in hazy countries and under faraway rain.

option.SOFT_BANDS=Soft bands
option.SOFT_BANDS.comment=How much light, the sky and the glow round the sun gather into gentle bands. 0 is a plain smooth gradient. There is never a hard edge or a dither pattern.
value.SOFT_BANDS.0=Off
suffix.SOFT_BANDS=%

option.DEBUG_VIEW=Debug view
option.DEBUG_VIEW.comment=Shows one of the shader's inner pictures instead of the world. For testing only.
value.DEBUG_VIEW.0=Off
value.DEBUG_VIEW.1=Depth
value.DEBUG_VIEW.2=Normals
value.DEBUG_VIEW.3=Light map
value.DEBUG_VIEW.4=Colour before light
