value.DEBUG_VIEW.12=Sun and shadows
value.DEBUG_VIEW.13=Ambient occlusion and far shadows
value.DEBUG_VIEW.14=Light through leaves
value.DEBUG_VIEW.15=Shadow, raw
value.DEBUG_VIEW.16=Shadow, smoothed
value.DEBUG_VIEW.17=Shadow history
value.DEBUG_VIEW.21=Terrain light

option.BRIDGE_MODE=VOID Gloam link
option.BRIDGE_MODE.comment=Normal reads live data from VOID Gloam. Backup only reads the coarser backup copy, as if the link had failed. Off ignores Gloam. For testing only.
value.BRIDGE_MODE.0=Normal
value.BRIDGE_MODE.1=Backup only
value.BRIDGE_MODE.2=Off

option.MIST_FORCE=Force mist
option.MIST_FORCE.comment=Forces the mist's time of day to this share, to see the slab at any hour. 0 leaves VOID Gloam's value. For testing only.
value.MIST_FORCE.0=Off
suffix.MIST_FORCE=%

option.DEBUG_JOIN=Show the far land join
option.DEBUG_JOIN.comment=Draws a magenta line along the join between the near chunks and the far land from VOID LOD, over the finished picture. For testing only.

option.HAZE_DEBUG=Haze debug
option.HAZE_DEBUG.comment=Haze test views: the country map, how thick the haze is, where the data came from, and wet ground with puddles.
value.HAZE_DEBUG.0=Off
value.HAZE_DEBUG.1=Haze kinds
value.HAZE_DEBUG.2=Haze thickness
value.HAZE_DEBUG.3=Data source
value.HAZE_DEBUG.4=Wet and puddles

option.SKY_DEBUG=Sky debug
option.SKY_DEBUG.comment=Sky test views: the sky colour table, or the sky's bands and rings.
value.SKY_DEBUG.0=Off
value.SKY_DEBUG.1=Sky table
value.SKY_DEBUG.2=Bands

# ---- Light: shadows (A)
option.SHADOW_FILTER=Soft shadow filter
option.SHADOW_FILTER.comment=Natural soft shadows, smoothed so no grain shows, or the older fixed filter. For testing only.
value.SHADOW_FILTER.0=Fixed (old)
value.SHADOW_FILTER.1=Natural
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS=Contact shadows
option.CONTACT_SHADOWS.comment=Small shadows the shadow map is too coarse to see: grass blades shading their own tufts, the lip of a stair, small gaps further off.
option.SHADOW_LONG_FADE=Long shadows at sunset
option.SHADOW_LONG_FADE.comment=In the last minutes before sunset, very long shadows from hills and woods far off thin out with their length, so the golden hour lasts until the sun touches the horizon. Full length keeps every shadow whole.
value.SHADOW_LONG_FADE.0=Full length
value.SHADOW_LONG_FADE.1=A little
value.SHADOW_LONG_FADE.2=Some
value.SHADOW_LONG_FADE.3=More
value.SHADOW_LONG_FADE.4=Most
option.TEMPORAL_LIGHT=Steadier light
option.TEMPORAL_LIGHT.comment=Blends the shadows with the last frames' to smooth them further. The smoothing never touches textures.
option.SHADOW_REFERENCE=Shadow reference
option.SHADOW_REFERENCE.comment=Draws the noise-free reference of the soft shadows: every noise value averaged at each pixel. Slow. For the grain check only.
option.TERRAIN_SHADOWS=Terrain shadows
option.TERRAIN_SHADOWS.comment=Hills and ridges shade the land behind them as far as 2 km off, even from off the screen, and slopes turned from the sun lie in their own shade. Needs VOID Gloam.
option.TERRAIN_SLOPE=Terrain slopes
option.TERRAIN_SLOPE.comment=How strongly the far land's slopes take the sun by how they face it: a hillside turned to a low sun glows, one turned away dims. 100 % is the land's true slope; more steepens it, as a map's hill shading does.
value.TERRAIN_SLOPE.0=Off
value.TERRAIN_SLOPE.100=True slope
value.TERRAIN_SLOPE.150=150 %
value.TERRAIN_SLOPE.200=200 %
value.TERRAIN_SLOPE.250=250 %
value.TERRAIN_SLOPE.300=300 %
value.TERRAIN_SLOPE.400=400 %

# ---- Light: ambient (B)
option.AO_STRENGTH=Occlusion strength
option.AO_STRENGTH.comment=How deep corners, the feet of walls, the inside of crowns and the roots of grass sink into shade. 1.25 is the pack's own depth; the shade never goes black.
option.AO_QUALITY=Occlusion quality
option.AO_QUALITY.comment=How many directions and steps the ambient occlusion looks along. High is a little smoother in deep corners and costs more.
value.AO_QUALITY.1=Normal
value.AO_QUALITY.2=High
option.AO_REFERENCE=Occlusion reference
option.AO_REFERENCE.comment=Draws the noise-free reference of the ambient occlusion: every noise value averaged at each pixel. Slow. For the grain check only.
option.AO_SUN_FAR=Far land's own shade
option.AO_SUN_FAR.comment=Past the shadow map's reach, and over the far land, the ambient occlusion also tells where the sun cannot get in: the floor between a far wood's crowns, the shaded side of a gully, the far wall of a hollow at a low sun. Soft, worked out from the shapes on screen. 0 leaves the far land's sun to the far shadows alone.
value.AO_SUN_FAR.0=Off
suffix.AO_SUN_FAR=%
option.FAR_LEAF_FORM=Far woods' form
option.FAR_LEAF_FORM.comment=Past the shadow map, how much more the far woods' leaves take the sun by how squarely they face it, on top of the leaves' own form. 0 keeps the leaves' own form alone.
value.FAR_LEAF_FORM.0=Off
suffix.FAR_LEAF_FORM=%
value.DEBUG_VIEW.18=Ambient occlusion
value.DEBUG_VIEW.19=Bent normals
value.DEBUG_VIEW.20=Sky light by direction
value.DEBUG_VIEW.22=Far land's own shade
# ---- Light: foliage (C)
option.LEAF_TRANSLUCENCY=Light through leaves
option.LEAF_TRANSLUCENCY.comment=How strongly sunlit leaves glow when you look toward the sun through a crown. The thin edges of a crown glow; its heart stays dark.
value.LEAF_TRANSLUCENCY.0=Off
suffix.LEAF_TRANSLUCENCY=%
option.PLANT_ROOT_SHADE=Plant roots
option.PLANT_ROOT_SHADE.comment=How much grass, flowers and crops darken toward their roots, so a meadow keeps its depth. 0 lights a tuft evenly.
value.PLANT_ROOT_SHADE.0=Off
suffix.PLANT_ROOT_SHADE=%

# ---- Light: air and tone (D)
option.AIR_MIE=Glow toward the sun
option.AIR_MIE.comment=The haze scatters the sun's light forward, so the air toward a low sun glows warm and bright over the far land and along the horizon, and stays plain away from it. A smooth gradient of the air itself, no bloom.
value.AIR_MIE.0=Off
suffix.AIR_MIE=%
option.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE=Aerial perspective
option.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE.comment=Past the near land, the land's colours lean toward the air's hue with distance and give up a little contrast (more toward a low sun), so hills and woods stand in layers. Not a veil: the land keeps its brightness.
value.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE.0=Off
suffix.AERIAL_PERSPECTIVE=%
option.SUN_SHAFTS=Sun shafts
option.SUN_SHAFTS.comment=At a low sun, beams of sunlit air between trunks and through gaps in the woods, and the long shadows of hills streaking the air. Subtle and smooth, never a fog; nearly nothing at noon. Needs Sun and moon shadows.
option.SHAFT_STRENGTH=Sun shaft strength
option.SHAFT_STRENGTH.comment=How bright the sun shafts are.
suffix.SHAFT_STRENGTH=%
option.WF_DEBUG=Far weather debug
option.WF_DEBUG.comment=Test views for far weather.
value.WF_DEBUG.0=Off
value.WF_DEBUG.1=Tiles
value.WF_DEBUG.2=Rain depth
value.WF_DEBUG.3=Far mist depth
value.WF_DEBUG.4=Far haze
option.UG_DEBUG=Underground debug
option.UG_DEBUG.comment=Draws the cave map from VOID Gloam on screen, with the cave state as bars. For testing only.
value.UG_DEBUG.0=Off
value.UG_DEBUG.1=On
option.WS_DEBUG=Water and shadow debug
option.WS_DEBUG.comment=Test views for water and shadows.
value.WS_DEBUG.0=Off
value.WS_DEBUG.1=Water normals
value.WS_DEBUG.2=Sun visibility
value.WS_DEBUG.3=Wet shores
value.WS_DEBUG.4=Season factors
